# Attachment upload = encrypt.lu single PUT (find the delta)

encrypt.lu proves Safari can PUT ~22 MiB in one XHR when the hop is equivalent.
Do **not** treat “Safari needs 1 MiB chunks” as the main story.

## Primary recipe (always on)

| Requirement | Value |
|---|---|
| Page | `https://privatenote.ai` (not `*.pages.dev`, not staging for the A/B) |
| Upload | `https://upload.privatenote.ai` |
| Transport | **XHR** `xhr.send(Blob)` (credentials omit) |
| Body | one untyped Blob |
| Method | PUT `/api/notes/:id/file` |
| Auth | `?uploadToken=` query only (no `Authorization` Bearer) |
| Proxy | never Pages `/api` for the binary body |

Staging QA hop (same recipe, different hosts):
`https://premium.privatenote.ai` → `https://upload-staging.privatenote.ai`

## Fast A/B (do this once)

Same Mac Safari, same ~22 MiB file:

1. encrypt.lu → one PUT, ~<3 s, 200
2. privatenote.ai → upload.privatenote.ai → same shape

If (2) fails: compare request headers with (1); check CF on **upload.privatenote.ai** (Bot Fight, WAF, Access, rate limit).
If (2) works: staging/cross-site was the bug — ship prod path; keep chunking off.

If prod same-site still aborts in ~200 ms with no Worker log, the kill is **before** app code (browser or CF edge on the upload host).

## CORS (upload relay)

Match `relay.encrypt.lu`: echo Origin, Allow-Headers echo, Allow-Methods GET/POST/PUT/OPTIONS, Max-Age 86400, **no** Allow-Credentials, **no** Set-Cookie.

## Temporary chunking

`SAFARI_CHUNKING_ENABLED` defaults **false**. Re-enable only after prod same-site single PUT A/B fails and CF/CORS deltas are ruled out. Then: few ~4 MiB serial PUTs — not many 1 MiB POSTs.
